# site-and-community — the landing page grows three things: the W moves into a
# nav bar, an Upcoming section derives itself from the game's own release notes,
# and a short pitch explains what happens to a report after you send it.
#
# Lane law: this lane READS the game repo (patchNotes.ts, CAMPAIGN.md,
# mainMenu.ts) and writes nothing outside whomp-site. Every glob below is
# relative to the whomp-site worktree root.

# The new pure modules and their suites. The index page moves out of
# bin/generate.mjs for the same reason the wiki did: it is testable alone.
bin/upcoming.mjs
bin/index-page.mjs
tests/upcoming.test.mjs
tests/indexPage.test.mjs

# The one hunk in the shared generator: the index template is replaced by a call
# to bin/index-page.mjs, and arcCards grows an option so the landing page can
# stop printing hand-typed arc dates that are already in the past.
bin/generate.mjs

# Prose describing the surface that changed.
README.md

# Lane paperwork.
docs/claims/site-and-community.claims
docs/lane-reports/site-and-community.md

# NOT CLAIMED, deliberately: index.html and the rest of the generated output.
# The three game artifacts this generator verifies before it will run
# (game-data, tier-rankings, wiki-visuals) are all stale on whomp main today, so
# no lane can regenerate the site right now. See the lane report.
